1259:
When any driver is found with a motor vehicle parked or stopped in violation of any parking provision of this article, any police officer, or any civilian officer designated by the chief of police to issue parking violation notices as part of their official duties, shall take the name, address and driver's license number of the alleged violator and the registration number of the motor vehicle involved and shall issue, in writing, and serve personally upon the violator a notice and summons, that shall include:
(1) The date and time of the violation;
(2) The location of the violation;
(3) The amount of the fine;
(4) The date by which the fine shall be paid; and
(5) The manner and time in which the violation may be contested in court.

1267:
An unauthorized sale vehicle is hereby declared to be a public nuisance as it:
(1) Creates a visual blight;
(2) Increases traffic hazards due to its distractive nature;
(3) Poses a safety hazard to potential purchasers;
(4) Disturbs the peace and quiet of residential neighborhoods;
(5) Tends to attract other vendor types thereby creating a "flea market" atmosphere;
(6) Causes damage to public property due to curb jumping;
(7) Causes damage to private property due to accumulations of trash and traffic over unpaved surfaces;
(8) Fails to protect the legitimate interests of licensed vehicle dealers; or
(9) Fails to protect the public against fraudulent transactions.

